        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Ajanta Caves</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 200 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Buddhist monks, patrons and artisans in two phases: the first possibly under the Satavahana dynasty or the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a>, the second under donors at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakataka-dynasty">Vakataka</a> emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harishena">Harishena</a> (Harisena), including his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varahadeva">Varahadeva</a> and the sub-king Upendragupta</span></div>
