          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where it is now</span><span class="info-stat-val">The northern wall of the U-shaped gorge of the River Waghur on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-plateau">Deccan Plateau</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangabad">Aurangabad</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>; copies of the paintings are held among others by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victoria-and-albert-museum">Victoria and Albert Museum</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Jataka scenes painted in Caves 1, 2, 16 and 17; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bodhisattva">bodhisattvas</a> Padmapani and Vajrapani in Cave 1; the oldest surviving ancient Indian murals in Caves 10 and 11; the stupa-fronted Buddha in Caves 19 and 26; Spink's disputed brief chronology; the tiger-hunting party of 1819</span></div>
